# Shared Component Parity (Laravel Blade)

> Every public page extends `resources/views/layouts/bdgs.blade.php`.
> Shared chrome lives in `resources/views/partials/bdgs/` — one edit updates every page.
> Do not copy-paste header/footer/modal/nav/FAB into page views.

---

## 1. Canonical Source of Truth

| Component | Canonical source | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Layout shell | `resources/views/layouts/bdgs.blade.php` | All pages `@extends('layouts.bdgs')` |
| Header + nav | `resources/views/partials/bdgs/header.blade.php` | `$activeNav` controls `active-page` class |
| Footer | `resources/views/partials/bdgs/footer.blade.php` | 4 columns + badges |
| Mobile nav | `resources/views/partials/bdgs/mobile-nav.blade.php` + `mobile-nav-scripts.blade.php` | Drilldown panels |
| Inquiry modal | `resources/views/partials/bdgs/inquiry-modal.blade.php` | Function `bdgsOpenInquiryModal()` in `shell-scripts.blade.php` |
| FAB | `resources/views/partials/bdgs/copy-page-fab.blade.php` + `copy-page-fab-scripts.blade.php` | Split button v4 with `cpb-fab__icon-open` |
| Shell CSS | `public/css/bdgs-shell.css` | Loaded by layout |
| FAB CSS | `public/css/cpb-fab.css` | Loaded by layout when FAB shown |

**Build a NEW page:** extend `layouts.bdgs`, set `@php($activeNav = '...')` only if the page is a top-nav item, add meta/title/schema in `index.blade.php`, body in `content.blade.php`. See `site-structure.mdc`.

**Homepage FAB delta:** Homepage sets `@php($showFab = false)` — layout omits FAB. All other standard pages show FAB via layout default.

---

## 2. Allowed Deltas (NOT drift)

| Delta | Rule |
|---|---|
| `$activeNav` / `active-page` | Set only on pages that match a top-nav item (`services`, etc.). Omit for pages not in top nav (e.g. `/webinars`). |
| Logo `<img>` attrs | `loading="lazy"` on standard pages; LCP page may use `fetchpriority="high"`. |
| `@section('ai-summary')` | Per-page AI summary override when content differs from default partial. |
| `$showFab = false` | Homepage only — no FAB. |
| Page-specific CSS | `public/css/bdgs-{slug}.css` via `@push('page-styles')`. |
| Page-specific JS | `@push('page-scripts')` — never re-declare shell modal/nav handlers. |

Everything else — structure, class names, dropdown contents, footer links, modal field set, FAB wiring — MUST come from the partials, not be duplicated in page views.

---

## 3. Parity Gate — run on every CREATE and every UPDATE that touches shared regions

Before a page can be marked done / locked:

1. **Confirm** `resources/views/pages/{slug}/index.blade.php` contains `@extends('layouts.bdgs')`.
2. **Confirm** the page does NOT embed header, footer, mobile nav, inquiry modal, or FAB markup inline in `content.blade.php`.
3. **Confirm** `$activeNav` is set correctly (or omitted for non-nav pages).
4. **Confirm** `bdgsOpenInquiryModal()` is used (never `bdgsOpenModal` or a page-local fork).
5. **One-time partial check** (when partials change): grep partials for `bdgsownv2-dropdown-mega`, `bdgs-mob-hamburger`, `cpb-fab__icon-open`, `bdgsOpenInquiryModal(`.
6. **Flag any divergence** not in §2, then ask the user before rewriting locked partials.

### Quick self-check greps (partials — run once when partials change)

- `bdgsownv2-dropdown-mega` present (mega-menu)
- `bdgs-mob-hamburger` + `bdgs-mob-panel` present (mobile drilldown)
- `cpb-fab__icon-open` present in `copy-page-fab.blade.php`
- `bdgsOpenInquiryModal(` present in `shell-scripts.blade.php`; `bdgsOpenModal(` absent
- Footer has 4 columns + `bdgsownv2-footer-badge` badges

### Per-page quick check

- `@extends('layouts.bdgs')` in `index.blade.php`
- No `<header class="bdgsownv2-header"` in `content.blade.php`
- No `<footer class="bdgsownv2-footer"` in `content.blade.php`

---

## 4. When you find drift

If a page embeds shell markup inline:

1. **Delete** the inline shell from `content.blade.php`.
2. **Ensure** the page extends `layouts.bdgs`.
3. If the shell partial itself is wrong, fix the **partial** (not one page copy).
4. Run the §3 parity gate.

Do **not** clone HTML from legacy static files.

